    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1bdc8449_968cb492",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/compat/OverrideValidatorImpl.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 80,
      "author": {
        "id": 1061116
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-23T13:20:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe the API name is not right. The Binder.getCallingUid isn\u0027t in all cases the right caller. In particular if you perform a recheck as part of app update you come from a different call path.",
      "parentUuid": "8e08466f_3e1bb4a5",
      "revId": "645ba4de9034d1a74197d3705270ac257edf7ddc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b1f8129a_251cae51",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/compat/OverrideValidatorImpl.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 80,
      "author": {
        "id": 1431994
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-24T16:50:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What would that call path be? I\u0027d still prefer we restrict what sort of callers can do this.",
      "parentUuid": "1bdc8449_968cb492",
      "revId": "645ba4de9034d1a74197d3705270ac257edf7ddc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "86d726d0_570680e5",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/compat/OverrideValidatorImpl.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 80,
      "author": {
        "id": 1061116
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-24T16:54:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Everything goes out of the window if we use a separate permission check, things become a lot simpler from there.\n\nThe callpath I am thinking of is:\n\nInstaller package sets override on installed package -\u003e callingUid is worked through, all good.\nOverride is stored.\nApp gets updated and recheck override is triggered.\nNow in order to validate again that the original caller is allowed to set those overrides we need the original caller, but they didn\u0027t trigger the recheck, so we need to store their uid somewhere and inject it into here.",
      "parentUuid": "b1f8129a_251cae51",
      "revId": "645ba4de9034d1a74197d3705270ac257edf7ddc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1fbaa5f8_6b521a86",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/compat/OverrideValidatorImpl.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 80,
      "author": {
        "id": 1431994
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-24T17:12:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, the first time the override is added, the call path will go through OverridevalidatorImpl ; the second time it will be through CompatConfig.recheckOverrides (and currently that eventually ends up in the same place).\nWhat if instead of storing the uid that made the initial override call, we just store a boolean that remembers whether the initial caller was the installer itself (or had the adequate permission)?",
      "parentUuid": "86d726d0_570680e5",
      "revId": "645ba4de9034d1a74197d3705270ac257edf7ddc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2624324b_490f1eec",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/compat/OverrideValidatorImpl.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 80,
      "author": {
        "id": 1061116
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-24T17:48:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are two things:\na) What\u0027s the benefit of storing the boolean over the uid? In that case, we could also just assume that the override got here because the original caller was allowed to and not recheck in the future.\n\nb) There is a case where an app gets updated by a different installer (as happened in the CTS tests). Storing a uid we can recheck, but storing a boolean we cannot. Now this is a bit of an edge case",
      "parentUuid": "1fbaa5f8_6b521a86",
      "revId": "645ba4de9034d1a74197d3705270ac257edf7ddc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "32c98f57_300a4838",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/compat/OverrideValidatorImpl.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 80,
      "author": {
        "id": 1431994
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-24T18:52:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What\u0027s the use case for re-checking? If you have to re-check upon update, I don\u0027t see any reason to ever store overrides beyond the current version.\n\nI don\u0027t like the idea of sending over the UID in the call in this case, as it can be easily spoofed, and I\u0027d quite frankly prefer not to store any extra information.\n\nIf the use case you have in mind is more complex, feel free to reach out off-CL in either chat or e-mail.",
      "parentUuid": "2624324b_490f1eec",
      "revId": "645ba4de9034d1a74197d3705270ac257edf7ddc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cb687c19_b7b91b98",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/compat/OverrideValidatorImpl.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 80,
      "author": {
        "id": 1061116
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-25T12:40:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Rechecking is a pre-existing concept in the code (I believe to catch going from debuggable to release apk). So in order to pass that check we need something to prove that this is a legit override. We could pass a boolean to say that this is a recheck and allow all overridable changes to go through under the premise that they would have been previously rejected if not allowed. wdyt?\n\nRe spoofing: I see your concern in general, but in this specific case the call goes system_server -\u003e system_server, so not sure how one would spoof that in the middle. I believe the only other user of IOverrideValidator is Settings and that\u0027s \u0027just\u0027 to show in the UI whether the change can be manipulated. It will eventually get checked again internally when the user tries to toggle. We could add a method to impl only and not expose on the aidl. Would that make things easier?",
      "parentUuid": "32c98f57_300a4838",
      "revId": "645ba4de9034d1a74197d3705270ac257edf7ddc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7cd7aa87_078dc08c",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/compat/OverrideValidatorImpl.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 80,
      "author": {
        "id": 1431994
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-25T14:56:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Re-check is not for going from debuggable to release (I actually kind of regret adding a test for that transition, since it\u0027s technically impossible). The re-check logic is for these cases:\n- app install, in which case overrides added pre-install get validated against the policy\n- app update, in which case existing changes could be invalidated if the targetSdk of the app is greater than the ones for specific compat changes\n- app uninstall, in which case existing changes become \u0027deferred\u0027 (i.e. to be re-checked on app install)\n\nThe question is how do we treat this new override mechanism; the way I see it, the extension to the existing policy is that a change id can ALSO be overridden if:\n- it has the @Overridable annotation\n- the caller has a - as of yet unnamed - permission when calling into the compat framework to be allowed to override\n- the override satisfies all the other existing constraints (except those related to the app\u0027s or operating system\u0027s debuggability)\n\nWhat I am recommending is that at override time, we save those two first conditions (really, the \u0026\u0026 of them); on recheck, the change is that you pass initial policy gate if `os.isdebuggable || app.isdebuggable || override_was_added_by_privileged_caller_on_overridable_change` (excuse the very weak pseudocode).",
      "parentUuid": "cb687c19_b7b91b98",
      "revId": "645ba4de9034d1a74197d3705270ac257edf7ddc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "39357b9f_8ee1c350",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/compat/OverrideValidatorImpl.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 80,
      "author": {
        "id": 1061116
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-25T15:07:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay. That makes sense.\nDo we really need to save anything in that case? Can\u0027t we take that fact that the override is here as proof that the original caller had the required permission?",
      "parentUuid": "7cd7aa87_078dc08c",
      "revId": "645ba4de9034d1a74197d3705270ac257edf7ddc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7ca64e2d_2cf84fb3",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/compat/OverrideValidatorImpl.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 80,
      "author": {
        "id": 1431994
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-25T15:50:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You could _probably_ manage that; not sure what weird scenarios we could concoct - i.e. if an override is added pre-install, or overrides are only applicable to versions outside the app\u0027s current version, and then it gets updated, etc.",
      "parentUuid": "39357b9f_8ee1c350",
      "revId": "645ba4de9034d1a74197d3705270ac257edf7ddc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
